calamares-settings-snapshot (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * welcome.conf: require 3 GiB of RAM instead of 1 GiB. The LUKS2 format of
    the root runs cryptsetup with Argon2id, which takes up to 1 GiB (half the
    RAM on a 2 GiB machine) on top of a live session that already uses about
    1.3 GB and has no swap. On a 2 GiB VMware Fusion VM the kernel killed
    cryptsetup for lack of memory. KPMcore's helper, which runs cryptsetup, is
    started by the system D-Bus daemon and lives in dbus.service, so systemd
    stopped the system bus; LightDM restarted without logind and the new
    session showed "Unable to contact settings server" (dbus-launch). The
    install never got past formatting. The welcome page now stops a machine
    with less than 3 GiB before anything is written.

 -- "Blackbird Cyber, LLC" <293711495+matthew-blackbird-cyber@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0400

